From 2d445cfa1c6f64495512d226ccb7d7e2afe5d651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:48:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix native Android login to handle 2FA and email verification

The native Compose login/register screens (NativeActivity is the app's
launcher) assumed every /api/auth/login and /api/auth/register response
carried a session straight away. The backend's instructor 2FA and student
email-verification work introduced three other 2xx shapes with no `user`
field at all (mfaSetupRequired, mfaRequired, pendingVerification) plus a
needsVerification flag on a 403 - AuthResponse.user was non-nullable, so
decoding any of these threw a serialization exception and the user was
stuck on a generic "something went wrong" error with no way to sign in.

Also fixes a second, independent bug this surfaced: the shared Retrofit
Json applies JsonNamingStrategy.SnakeCase globally, but the auth endpoints
are hand-written camelCase object literals (mfaRequired, challengeId,
emailVerified, ...), not DB-row passthroughs - so even with a nullable
user, every one of those fields would have silently decoded to its
default (false/null) without explicit @SerialName overrides. This also
means User.emailVerified has never actually decoded correctly.

- AuthResponse/User/request models: nullable user, new mfa/verification
  fields, @SerialName on every camelCase multi-word field.
- ApiService/AuthRepository: added mfa/verify and resend-verification
  calls; login/register now return the full response so the UI can branch.
- LoginViewModel/LoginScreen: new states and UI for email-verification
  notice (with resend) and TOTP setup/challenge/backup-codes, mirroring
  the web app's login.js + mfa.js flow.
- RegisterViewModel/RegisterScreen: handles pendingVerification with a
  "check your email" + resend screen instead of assuming instant login.
- LoginRequest: portal defaults to "public" (matching the web app) instead
  of an unrecognized "student" value that was silently bypassing the
  backend's "admin sign-in not available here" check.

